# lsfg-vk — the HOST aarch64 Vulkan layer, built FROM SOURCE via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD
# (packages/lsfg-vk/PKGBUILD), NOT fetched from the holo monorepo: the curated holo aarch64 repos
# ship no lsfg-vk at all, and upstream publishes no arm64 binary either (builds.lsfg-vk.dev carries
# x86_64 and i686 only). So there is nothing to `pacman -S` and nothing to download; we build it.
#
# WHY IT IS NEEDED despite every game here being x86: a Proton title's Vulkan calls are thunked out
# to the HOST arm64 driver by Valve's compat tool, and pressure-vessel imports implicit layers from
# the host's /usr/share/vulkan/implicit_layer.d. A layer must match the driver it fronts, so
# Proton coverage needs an aarch64 layer installed host-side. The x86 layer
# (packages/lsfg-vk-x86) covers the OTHER paths -- system FEX and native x86-64 Linux titles under
# the compat tool, which render on the guest x86 Turnip. The two are complementary, not
# alternatives. Measured on HW 2026-08-30; see the PKGBUILD header and issue #81.
#
# NO `patches:` LINE, EVER. lsfg-vk is CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 and NoDerivatives means we may not ship a
# modified build. Wanting to add one here is the signal to talk to upstream instead --
# .claude/plans/lsfg-vk-upstream-outreach.md asks about exactly this build.
#
# Fields (see packages/mangohud/source.pin for the same shape):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to pkgrel so pacman prefers our build
#
# To bump: edit pkgver AND _rev in the PKGBUILD together (_rev is the upstream commit -- currently
# a master snapshot rather than a tag; the PKGBUILD header says why), then re-run
# packages/lsfg-vk/probe-benchmark.sh -- the per-SoC flow-scale defaults the Decky plugin ships are
# measured, not derived.
name: lsfg-vk
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
